  "body": "Parent: [#6019](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/6019) (semi-automated ingestion operations). Research source: prior-art doc `~/workspace/scratch/atlas-ingestion-brief-2026-11-04/prior-art-research.md` (2026-11-04). Follow-up 43 (Cluster 7). Consumer: the retention rule engine (sibling under #6026).\n\n## Finding (research, in substance)\n\nVersioned-corpus growth ≈ Σ over sources of (churn bytes/day × avg versions retained). With span reuse, a version's *marginal* storage is only its new spans + manifest — so the model's inputs (per-source churn, reuse ratio, version counts) are all measurable from the ingest ledger (sibling cost-ledger design under #6019) after a few weeks of operation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- The model: per-source churn × retention → hot/cold storage projection vs the plan envelope (#6019's ceiling: Turso scaler $24.92/mo today; storage + DB-count quotas bind before embedding spend).\n- Calibration loop: v1 retention defaults start **conservative (keep more)**; the model recalibrates from real churn before any deletion policy fires; cold-tier moves precede deletions by at least one full retention cycle.\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA growth model + the calibration procedure that turns ledger data into retention defaults for #6026's rule engine.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=muse state=filed source=main-chat-2026-11-04-wave2 -->",
